-- RW1 (#308): the planned nodes, re-planned for the 13600 world.
--
-- The rural ring widened to r4600 and the wilds moved out to r4600 to r6800
-- (rural plan RD10), so the plan changed everywhere past the suburb: the
-- rural ring's woods, branches, outcrops and veins cover twice the ground,
-- the wilds grow on new land, and every zone's nodes now keep off the wild
-- water where it runs onto the plain (`node_spawn::plan_with`), so no move
-- migration follows, as #222's did.
--
-- This replaces every planned row rather than adding to them: every node of
-- a planned type goes, from E2.3's (20261106), W6's and #225's (20261113,
-- 20261114) and #222's moves of them (20261112), and the new plan comes in.
-- The seeded grass isn't planned, and stays, moved by the first set's
-- 20261122_001_rural_widens.sql with everything else. Nothing a player
-- owns is a node, so no owner loses one; a node half gathered starts over.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_new_nodes` run with
-- `PRINT_ALL_NODES=1`, and `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks
-- they still match the plan.
--
--   clay_bank in suburban: 36
--   clay_bank in urban: 42
--   clay_bank in wilderness: 315
--   copper_vein in wilderness: 788
--   fallen_branches in rural: 573
--   fallen_branches in suburban: 72
--   fallen_branches in wilderness: 2364
--   iron_vein in rural: 19
--   iron_vein in wilderness: 630
--   old_growth in wilderness: 4727
--   reed_bed in wilderness: 473
--   rock_outcrop in rural: 229
--   rock_outcrop in wilderness: 1576
--   tin_vein in wilderness: 315
--   tree in rural: 951
DELETE FROM resource_nodes
WHERE resource_type IN ('tree', 'old_growth', 'fallen_branches', 'rock_outcrop', 'iron_vein', 'copper_vein',
                        'tin_vein', 'clay_bank', 'reed_bed');

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
